  "behavior": [
    "External EVM message and typed-data completion recovers the signer using the same admitted byte/schema helpers and compares it with the queued account.",
    "External eth_sendTransaction completion is rejected: an arbitrary hash cannot prove the reviewed transaction fields. The normal local/mobile send path remains separate.",
    "Substrate raw bytes require the exact wrapBytes contract and matching decoded payload/account identities. Verification deliberately does not accept the generic library wrapped/unwrapped fallback.",
    "Version-4 extrinsics use a fresh registry with current matching metadata, the same method-without-length-prefix encoding, a Blake2 prehash only over 256 bytes, and exact MultiSignature enum routing. Unsupported versions reject.",
    "Verification is synchronous after the existing phishing, request ownership and authorization/context guards. Invalid completion consumes the request without key export, network transport or signature release."
  ],
